# Bug: `kanso check lib` accepts a library that `kanso check main.kso`
# refuses, and the refusal prints no source line.
#
# Run from this directory: kanso check lib; kanso check main.kso
#
# should: the same verdict from both. `made` stores a `text/slice` that can be
#   none (ruling 2026-10-13, #1890) in a record field, and `path_key s.path`
#   hands it to a function with no none arm.
# does: `kanso check lib` prints `lib: ok`. `kanso check main.kso` (and so
#   run and build) prints "error[exhaustive]: this can be a none and
#   `lib/path_key` has no arm for it ... --> lib/lib.kso:15:48" and stops
#   there: the line excerpt and caret every other diagnostic shows are
#   missing. In the toml port the same refusal also named the wrong module,
#   "(module cli)", for a line in toml/table.kso.

import "./lib"

print "{lib/spelled [["a" "b" "c"]]}"
